' ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
' LEGEND
' ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

legend right
  |= Symbol      |= Meaning                                                   |
  | component    | Black-box implementation unit (a class or cohesive cluster)|
  | lollipop ()  | Provided interface (realised by the attached component)    |
  | ..>          | Required interface / dependency (injected at a composition root)|
  | «internal»   | Assembly-scoped interface; cross-team consumers may NOT bind|
  | «MonoBehaviour» | Unity ACL — touches UnityEngine within its package      |
  | «pure C# VM» | ViewModel with no UnityEngine import                       |
  | (decl STn — realised STm) | Interface DECLARED by one team, REALISED by another |
  ----
  All seven sub-teams are now skeleton-ported (info/README.md). Cross-team
  contracts are declared by their owning team and realised wherever the
  concrete lives — e.g. IVolumeDataSet is ST1-declared, ST3-realised
  (Rendering/VolumeDataSet); IDesktopShell is ST1-declared, ST6-realised
  (UI/CanvassDesktop). «internal» interfaces stay inside their owning
  assembly per DD-5.
  ST5 VR menu shells (FeatureMenuController/Cell, MomentMapMenuController,
  SpectralProfileHelper) and the ST3 HistogramMenuController live physically
  under UI/ but are owned by ST5 / ST3.
  Realisers absent from the skeleton (built at a composition root): concrete
  IVolumeRegistry / IVolumeLoader (Kernel Bootstrap), RenderSettings POCO
  (IRenderSettings/Mutator/IRenderStateCapture/IRestFrequencyCatalogue),
  IFitsMaskWriter / IFitsCubeReader, IVolumeStateCapture, ILogSink
  (DebugLogging, Tier-3).
endlegend

